  "answer": "**Final status: passing.** On the second verification run (`20261021T114945Z-ac1d69`), all three configured stages passed: build, unit and component. It took one fix cycle.\n\n**What failed:** On the first run (`20261021T114859Z-5bf7d9`) the build passed but the unit stage failed (exit code 2), so the component stage was skipped. One test failed on both net9.0 and net10.0: `DeltaFormatterTests.Format_FieldInActualNotInExpected_ShowsAbsentSentinel`.\n\n**Root cause:** When the actual response has a field the expected body doesn't, the failure output is supposed to label it `<absent>`. The code in `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs` used `<not present>` instead. The test was right, not the code: `doc/failure-output.md` and the matching spec both say `<absent>`.\n\n**What was changed:** One line in `src/ConfIT/Matching/DeltaFormatter.cs:69`:\n```diff\n-                expected = TestColor.Subtle(\"<not present>\");\n+                expected = TestColor.Subtle(\"<absent>\");\n```\nNo tests were modified.\n\nThe verifier only ran the stages configured in `.lattice/verification.yaml`. Integration tests and the skills check (`make integration` / `make skills`) aren't among them, so they weren't run. Nothing was committed.",
